title: "Switch"
description: "An on and off toggle for a single setting, with variants, sizes, and rounded corners."
---

<script lang="ts">
	import Demo from "./demo.svelte";
</script>

# Switch

Turns a single setting on or off, and takes effect right away. It renders a `button` with `role="switch"` and `aria-checked`, so Space and Enter toggle it. Link a `Label` with `for` and give the switch the same `id`, so clicking the label toggles it too.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Switch } from "#lib/components/ui/switch/index.js";
	import { Label } from "#lib/components/ui/label/index.js";
</script>

<Switch id="airplaneMode" />
<Label for="airplaneMode">Airplane mode</Label>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/switch.json
```

## Controlled

Use `bind:checked` to read and set the state from your own code, or `onCheckedChange` to run code on each toggle. Without either, set `defaultChecked` to start the switch on.

<Demo section="controlled" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Switch } from "#lib/components/ui/switch/index.js";
	import { Label } from "#lib/components/ui/label/index.js";

	let isNotifying = $state(true);
</script>

<Switch id="notifications" bind:checked={isNotifying} />
<Label for="notifications">Notifications</Label>
<p>Notifications are {isNotifying ? "on" : "off"}.</p>
```

A passed `onclick` runs before the toggle. Call `e.preventDefault()` in it to keep the current state, such as while asking for confirmation.

## Forms

Set `name` to submit the switch with a form. Like a checkbox, it submits `value`, which defaults to `"on"`, only while the switch is on.

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<form method="POST">
	<Switch id="newsletter" name="newsletter" value="yes" />
	<Label for="newsletter">Subscribe to the newsletter</Label>
</form>
```

## Variants

Set `variant` to `default` or `destructive` to change the track color while the switch is on.

<Demo section="variants" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Switch variant="destructive" defaultChecked />
```

## Sizes

Set `size` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg`. The default is `md`, and the corner radius follows the size.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Switch size="lg" />
```

## Rounded

Set `rounded` to `xs` through `4xl` or `pill` to override the radius of the track and thumb. Use `pill` for a pill.

<Demo section="rounded" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Switch rounded="pill" />
```

## States

Set `disabled` to dim the switch and block toggling. Set `aria-invalid="true"` to show the invalid ring, such as for a required setting that is still off.

<Demo section="states" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Switch disabled />
<Switch aria-invalid="true" />
```

## API

The `Switch` props extend the native `button` attributes, and extra attributes such as `id` pass through to the button. The root and thumb set `data-state` to `checked` or `unchecked` for custom styles.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends CompProps<"button"> {
	/** Whether the switch is on; supports `bind:checked` */
	checked?: boolean;
	/** Starting state when `checked` is not set; defaults to `false` */
	defaultChecked?: boolean;
	/** Called with the new state when the switch is toggled */
	onCheckedChange?: (checked: boolean) => void;
	/** Form field name; submits `value` while the switch is on */
	name?: string;
	/** Value submitted with the form while on; defaults to `"on"` */
	value?: string;
	/** Color of the track while on */
	variant?: "default" | "destructive";
	/** Switch size on the shared scale; defaults to `md` */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Corner radius of the track and thumb; follows `size` when omitted */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}
```
